Technical architecture

Alva is built using:

* Vanilla JavaScript ES modules.
* HTML5 and CSS.
* Canvas 2D rendering.
* A deterministic, fixed-step game simulation.
* Dynamically loaded PNG character animation frames.
* Native keyboard, touch, and controller inputs.
* Browser localStorage for persistent settings.

There is currently no required build process, JavaScript framework, WebGL dependency, or runtime package dependency.

The main entry point is index.html, which loads js/main.js.

js/core/app.js initializes the application, managers, screens, settings, localization, and game loop.

The simulation is implemented across js/game/, with data-driven character definitions in js/data/characters/.

Understand these relationships before touching anything.

