This is an illustrative layout, not a mandatory naming contract.

The resulting production directory must contain every resource the game genuinely needs.

Preserve all required assets and their relative references.

Important distinction

There are two possible forms of consolidation:

A. Production bundling

Combining multiple source files into fewer distributable files without destroying or reorganizing the originals.

B. Source consolidation

Actually combining modules or stylesheets inside the development repository.

Prioritize A.

Only perform B when there is a clear architectural benefit, the merge is low risk, and all affected tests and references can be maintained without changing behavior.

Do not merge important gameplay modules merely to reduce the repository’s file count.

A production build is preferable to turning the original source into giant, difficult-to-maintain files.

