9. Create an itch.io-compatible production build

Create a clean, deployable HTML5 distribution.

Prefer an output structure such as:

dist/itch/index.html
dist/itch/game.js
dist/itch/game.css
dist/itch/assets/...
dist/itch/manifest.webmanifest

Include additional root assets and icons required by the existing game.

The production export must be self-contained.

Do not depend on fetching source files from GitHub, GitHub Pages, a development server, or another external host.

Do not require Node.js, npm, or any development tooling in the player’s browser.

All build tooling must run before distribution.

Path handling

All resource paths must work when the game is hosted:

* At a domain root.
* Under a nested subdirectory.
* Within an itch.io HTML5 embed.

Preserve correct case-sensitive paths.

Avoid hard-coded absolute paths.

Make sure the asset loader can still retrieve every required frame.

Validate that generated JavaScript and CSS paths point to real files.

Embedding

itch.io normally displays HTML5 games inside an iframe.

Test:

* Fullscreen launch.
* Embedded viewport sizing.
* Keyboard focus.
* Gamepad access where supported.
* Pointer and touch controls.
* Resizing.
* Landscape orientation.
* Pausing and resuming after focus changes.

Do not modify Alva’s gameplay rules to work around platform-specific restrictions.

If a browser or embedding limitation cannot be solved without changing the experience, document it separately.

PWA behavior

Alva already has a web app manifest and installation interface, implemented through js/core/web-app-install.js.

Keep the existing standalone installation behavior intact.

Test it separately from the itch.io embedded experience.

Do not introduce an offline service worker, storage changes, or a different installation system as part of this task.

